{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded","id":682380,"title":"Man, I love Dragon-Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-29T15:43:12-07:00","id":682380,"title":"Man, I love Dragon-Blooded","content":"Posters may remember that I love Solars. I love them as unironic heroes there to bring goodness and light to a world filled with myriad shades of darkness. They\u2019re the mighty saviors of the world; the Supermen, Thors, and Wonder Women whose very passing causes the world to shake.<br /> <br /> I also love (Imperial) Dragon-Blooded, and I love them because they\u2019re the antithesis of the Solars. I see them as far more of a foil/counterpart than the Abyssals or Infernals ever were.<br /> <br /> What do I mean? (This is going to be obvious to many of you.)<br /> <br /> The Solars are the new-kid on the block. The Dragon-Blooded and the Realm are the established power.<br /> <br /> While a Solar is often a wanderer with no built in organization, Dragon-Blooded are born and raised in Creation\u2019s premiere powerblock. At the same time, Solars are likely to create their own organizations \u2013 becoming warlords, merchant princes, or the like \u2013 while Dragon-Blooded are typically constrained within the institutions that birthed them.<br /> <br /> Solars are defined as the strongest while the Dragon-Blooded are the weakest. Yes, they\u2019re doing away with the tiers, but Solars are always going to stand at the pinnacle of Creation. Heck, they *define* what that pinnacle is. Dragon-Blooded are near the bottom in Creation, and are the weakest of the PC splats.<br /> <br /> And this creates an interesting paradox of power. The DB are the weakest, but they overthrew the strongest. The DB can simultaneously be the hegemonic authority and the scrappy underdog. The existence of the Realm means Solars can both be the God-Kings of Creation and the rebels fighting against the overwhelming might of the Empire.<br /> <br /> The Solars are the shining heroes while the Dragon-Blooded are always shades-of-grey. Even the most noble and good-hearted Dragon-Blooded are supporting a social system of exploitation, slavery, ruthless conquest, corrupt bureaucracy, and a false belief. Even the most decadent and cruel Dragon-Blooded is supporting the greatest civilization in the Second Age. one that\u2019s been instrumental in safe-guarding all of Creation for a couple thousand years.<br /> <br /> Also, I find Solars and Dragon-Blooded to be the most human of the splats, which I like, but that doesn\u2019t support my \u2018Dragon-Blooded are the antithesis of Solars,\u2019 so ignore that.<br /> <br /> Footnote 1: Please don\u2019t turn this into a thread about how my conception of Solars is bad and wrong.<br /> Footnote 2: I am specifically talking about Dragon-Blooded of the Blessed Realm who are part of a House. Outcastes are okay, but not half as interesting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T15:48:23-07:00","id":682409,"title":"","content":"At first I ignored the DB's because they were weaker, but you're right. There's so many juicy plots in the Realm waiting to be played out, and I just like big and elaborate bureaucratic clusterfucks and the Great Houses have those in <i>spades</i>.<br /> <br /> I disagree with your perception of Outcastes however. They provide another look at the Terrestrial Exaltation and have their own interesting plots--especially if they cross paths with the Realm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T15:51:14-07:00","id":682412,"title":"","content":"Honestly one of my biggest disappointments with the first two editions was that we didn't get nearly enough juicy details about the Great Houses. I really felt we could have used a Great Houses of the Realm book to help round out the houses and give good ideas on what members of a given house born and raised in different areas of the Realm might traditionally focus on and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T15:55:26-07:00","id":682414,"title":"","content":"I like the Realm Dragonbloods, but I love the Dragonblood of Lookshy. I love the military mentality of the Seventh Legion. The idea that Dragonbloods should use their powers to serve Creation rather than themselves. I even love the hypocrisy of a high restricted society that is built on the idea of Freedom. The Seventh Legion is one of the few groups that told the most powerful person in Creation to fuck off and get away with it. <br /> <br /> My Solar characters usually have a Dragonblooded Ally, because while Solars are the wandering heroes to bring light back to Creation, they still need an emotional connection to Creation. Dragonbloods make a good anchor for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T15:56:08-07:00","id":682415,"title":"","content":"Combining your footnotes, I agree with your idea of Solars, and I like Outcastes for much the same reason. Lost Eggs can be wandering heroes struggling to find their place in the world, battling monsters and villains, founding institutions and legacies, and generally being Exalted heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T16:02:01-07:00","id":682418,"title":"","content":"To date, my group has run a lot of games, here numbered by predominant splat involved (cross-splating is a sometimes-food):<br /> 1 Solar Game (all Solars)<br /> 1 Solar/Lunar (1 to 2, respectively)<br /> 2 Lunar (all Lunar)<br /> 0.5 + 0.5 Abyssal (both only one session long, so count as 1)<br /> 2 Infernals (al Infernals, both times)<br /> 1 Sidereal (two sessions)<br /> and........ 5 Dragonblooded. 2 involving lineages of characters.<br /> <br /> Lineages. I make a character, who does awesome things, and later an awesome kid comes about who is also playable. Dragonblooded.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T16:02:25-07:00","id":682419,"title":"","content":"I like mortals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What's this you were saying about the weakest splat, now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-29-2015, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T16:50:18-07:00","id":682439,"title":"","content":"Responding to Hippokrene's original post.<br /> <br /> Terrestrials are my favorite splat. I love all Exalts, but something about them strikes me as awesome. It's partly the whole Romance of the Three Kingdoms vibe they have, its also partly that they absolutely require the infrastructure they have built up. It makes them feel more attached to the setting and I love that.<br /> <br /> I do love outcastes as well but thats more cause winning the genetic lottery suddenly opening the entire world up for you is always a fun thing. (I play outcastes in that regard like a Solar, but without the fear of being an Anathema, and have managed to make a low bred outcaste the most useful member of an all celestials (1 solar, 2 abyssals and 1 lunar) party.<br /> <br /> I tend to make my outcastes young kids who get thrust into a story Link style. Growing up, suddenly no longer a kid, but expected to be a hero because you glow now. Always kinda fun.<br /> <br /> I don't like the idea &quot;they are weakest so they are useless&quot; mentality. I had a player in the exact game i mention who played a solar actively tell me OOC &quot;hey, yeah your DB is dragging us down and we need you to learn CMA so you can stay relevant...&quot;<br /> <br /> I love the whole political intrigue, the whole no matter how much you may be a big shot, there are a bunch of people pulling strings behind you. It feels good.<br /> <br /> So ,Yay to this thread. (And while Solars are my least favorite, I've had a lot of fun with them as well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1777,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","user":"Kell_Tamer","date":". 09-29-2015, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T16:50:42-07:00","id":682441,"title":"","content":"I think I'll be able to be insired with a lot for the Scarlet Dynasty from War and Peace, which I am attempting to read again after about... God, seven years. Already I have all kinds of insincere formal language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T17:02:34-07:00","id":682473,"title":"","content":"When we started playing Exalted, we pretty much played Dragonblood. I've played about 10 DB characters. For a while, it was actually odd when I started playing Solars/Lunars, and went &quot;wait, I'm playing Exalted, but we don't spend all our time at decadent parties intriguing and stabbing each other in the back? What's going on?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T17:27:39-07:00","id":682480,"title":"","content":"As someone to whom family has never had intrinsic value (by which I mean being family doesn't mean I have to like you, agree with you, or support you if you're being an ass), Dragon-Blooded, who are defined by their ancestry, intrigue me in a way I think I'm ill-equipped to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 09-29-2015, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T17:52:32-07:00","id":682490,"title":"","content":"I want to see what Dragonblooded can do when they're not getting Worfed on anymore. Looking forward to What Fire Has Wrought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T18:02:49-07:00","id":682498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded#post682380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Footnote 1: Please don\u2019t turn this into a thread about how my conception of Solars is bad and wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>curses foiled again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T18:40:31-07:00","id":682569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682480#post682480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone to whom family has never had intrinsic value (by which I mean being family doesn't mean I have to like you, agree with you, or support you if you're being an ass), Dragon-Blooded, who are defined by their ancestry, intrigue me in a way I think I'm ill-equipped to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, that's kind of funny because I'm from exactly the opposite kind of family but have the same reaction. The whole backstabbing your sister to get her stuff and advance your political career is just something that doesn't work for me, but feels like it's all over the place with Ream DBs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T18:44:24-07:00","id":682575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682480#post682480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone to whom family has never had intrinsic value (by which I mean being family doesn't mean I have to like you, agree with you, or support you if you're being an ass), Dragon-Blooded, who are defined by their ancestry, intrigue me in a way I think I'm ill-equipped to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682569#post682569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah, that's kind of funny because I'm from exactly the opposite kind of family but have the same reaction. The whole backstabbing your sister to get her stuff and advance your political career is just something that doesn't work for me, but feels like it's all over the place with Ream DBs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My parents were not very parental, yet family is a big part of my character background. I enjoy playing with backstabbing family NPCs and &quot;Don't you dare lay a hand on my little brother&quot; NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T18:58:39-07:00","id":682579,"title":"","content":"The Deadly Decadent court troupe is by and large one of my favorite. From the orleasians of Dragon Age to the warring houses and interplay of Game of Thrones I see Dragon-Blooded games being played and played well each time and while I have yet to play in or run one of these games (Its so hard for me to find a group :'( ) I absolutly love the idea of playing in a setting where my skill with words and politics are just as if not more important than my ability with a blade and Dragon-Blooded are the best splat I've found for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T19:40:16-07:00","id":682589,"title":"","content":"My sister is someone with whom I'd be comfortable playing 100% cooperate in a one-shot Prisoner's Dilemma.<br /> <br /> I still love DBs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T20:07:56-07:00","id":682598,"title":"","content":"I love Dragon-Blooded threads. This is the content that intrigues me most.<br /> <br /> I love the Terrestrial Exalted, the Realm, and all its trappings. Im a sucker for the established organized 'evil' religion, doing good and bad both for the safety of the world. I can hardly wait for the dragon blooded book, and my only regret is going to be not having an extra 500$ to throw at the kickstarter despite however much I pledge anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T20:22:33-07:00","id":682617,"title":"","content":"To what degree do you think the game should emphasize that the Realm is squatting on the ruins of a bigger empire the Host is physically incapable of operating or maintaining, like Kevin trying to stay at home after his parents forget him at home (but probably less insulting than that comparison)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T20:32:30-07:00","id":682621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682617#post682617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what degree do you think the game should emphasize that the Realm is squatting on the ruins of a bigger empire the Host is physically incapable of operating or maintaining, like Kevin trying to stay at home after his parents forget him at home (but probably less insulting than that comparison)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think there should be very little of this. That was more the Shogunate's bag. I feel like the most impressive structure in the Imperial City should be of terrestrial design. There should definitely be signs of the former age though. Like a city built on an imperishable first age breakwater with defensive emplacements or weather control that's beyond it's current owners, but maybe a Solar circle of PCs could get their hands on it and take over the port in a single move, or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T20:36:38-07:00","id":682623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682621#post682621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think there should be very little of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to fall on that side of it too--fuck reclaiming the past, how's about we build a little goddamned future, huh?--but a big theme of the game is post-apocalyptica, so I wondered how others feel.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T20:49:29-07:00","id":682625,"title":"","content":"I'd be quite happy to play a Dragonblood keen on bringing back the lost wonders of the Shogunate. But before that... well, that's of the Anathema, it's dark and forbidden sorcery, and should be treated as such (by which I mean, if you're playing a dodgy sorcerer who's willing to do morally ambiguous things, then go for it!). Righteous and upstanding Dragonblood should have no interest in building wonders on the blood of thousands of slaves as the Anathema presumably did!<br /> <br /> (Oh, and in a more general context: having played a Twilight, I have no interest in restoring the First Age, I'd rather build something new, like JimB said. But that might be because I found the First Age quite dull. If it was more interesting, maybe I'd be more interested)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T23:19:56-07:00","id":682691,"title":"","content":"There were two reasons I ignored Dragonblooded:<br /> <br /> 1) They mechanics were fucked, thus I did not want to deal with them (I don't mean power, but I mean their charms were total ass. Even 2.5e they're PLAYABLE at least)<br /> 2) I deal with so much family drama IRL that dealing with it in a game had no interest to me.<br /> <br /> However in 3e I would be an outcaste, assuming if their mechanics are non-fucked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T00:27:23-07:00","id":682725,"title":"","content":"We did tons of Dragonblood, and the charms generally work (you just have to ignore what Step the writer thought they were). They work better than Sid charms. Of course, they're kind of weak* in 2.0, but then, we were playing the weak Dragonblood.*<br /> 2.5 improves them, but going back and forth to check what's been errata'd is a big headache, and I was pretty much the only one who could remember what had changed most of the time.<br /> <br /> If you wanted the power, \u200bwell... that's what Sorcery and TMA were for (I remember some people said MA were supposed to be a bit weaker, ie CMA were weaker than Solar charms, but whoever wrote TMA obviously didn't get that memo!).<br /> <br /> *On the other hand, in 2e, they made up with it with free reflexives and dirt-cheap excellencies, which was excellent. Not to mention artefacts. When we first started playing Solars, a Fire-Aspected Dragonblood with Five-Dragon Style was absolutely terrifying. He can attack... and defend! At the same time! And he has first-age power armour<i> and </i>a jade direlance! On one guy! We actually ran away from Dragonblood most of the time. Once the whole party managed to take down one Fire-Aspect.<br /> <br /> Finally... I loved playing Dragonblood because the fights were much more enjoyable than Solar fights. No-one needed to paranoia combo, because combos are for Anathema chumps. And no one perfect-spammed because the perfects cost willpower, and had flaws that were actually real flaws. So people actually had a proper combat rather than perfect-spam(x20)+die.<br /> I guess in 2e though, Solars should be able to have fun fights too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T01:33:11-07:00","id":682799,"title":"","content":"Solars are my favorite splat, because they are a blank canvas. Anyone can become a Solar, they can have any outlook, etc.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are number 2 on my list because they come with so much baked in. I can toss so many levels of family strife, intrigue, and generational ambition on them, and it's gratifying to see it play out. I came to WW as a Vampire player, so I've always enjoyed games that are more than hack 'n slash. <br /> <br /> I also really enjoy the experience of my PC somewhat hoodwinked. Most of the Immaculate Doctrine is bullshit, but hey, it tells my PC that he's enlightened and can do no wrong. Sounds like fun!<br /> <br /> Finally, there is a certain monster-movie feel to them. Sure, they are tough, but if they run into an Anathema, they could get splatted. So, stick together, and with a lot of skill and a little luck, the PC Dragon-Bloods can triumph over a superior opponent.<br /> <br /> One thing I have not had the opportunity to do, and would really enjoy, is playing a Dragon-Blooded Dynast in a group of Celestials. Using my connections and savvy to keep up with people with a great deal more inherent power is my kind of challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T01:42:58-07:00","id":682830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682799#post682799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I have not had the opportunity to do, and would really enjoy, is playing a Dragon-Blooded Dynast in a group of Celestials. Using my connections and savvy to keep up with people with a great deal more inherent power is my kind of challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also really fun to do! Admittedly, in my group, we always even out the Experience Costs for the DBs to match the Solars... but even so, its a rough ride that forces you to bring your A-game if you want to remain relevant. And those few times you meet up with another Dragon-Blood and are able to combo Charms together in some unlikely instance... and its just impressive and fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T02:04:33-07:00","id":682838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682830#post682830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also really fun to do! Admittedly, in my group, we always even out the Experience Costs for the DBs to match the Solars... but even so, its a rough ride that forces you to bring your A-game if you want to remain relevant. And those few times you meet up with another Dragon-Blood and are able to combo Charms together in some unlikely instance... and its just impressive and fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done it once but the results were a little less than stellar for me. I've played DBs in mixed games before, which ended up being more fun, but the time I tried to play up the connections and infrastructure part of that it ended up flip flopping between a liability for the whole circle, and feeling like the rest of the party treated me like an ID badge in a sci-fi rpg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T02:50:20-07:00","id":682859,"title":"","content":"my first character in Exalted, was a Dragon-blooded. Water Aspect. was a mafia lord of a smuggling ring before he ever Exalted. too bad I never got far with him. perhaps when the DB book comes out I'll re-imagine him, try him again, hope he gets farther this time.<br /> <br /> other than that....I like the Dragon-Blooded, because they are detailed in ways that Solars are not. I can feel more part of the world than I do with a Solar. and just because I am not that much of a family person doesn't mean I cannot explore the themes- the one family member who is a black sheep, who doesn't agree with the rest of the family is exploring the theme as well. family is far from perfect after all. and honestly if they're all backstabbing jerks anyways....well then, that just shows how important &quot;family&quot; really is to them, doesn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T05:03:46-07:00","id":682999,"title":"","content":"The Houses (and of course the individuals therein) have different opinions and thresholds on what constitutes &quot;backstabbing.&quot; House Frey felt that Robb Stark backstabbed them by backing out of an arranged union to marry for love, but Robb almost certainly didn't do it thinking, &quot;Fuck those Freys, I don't need their alliance!&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, pretty much everyone but House Frey felt the Red Wedding took the whole &quot;backstabbing&quot; thing too far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-30-2015, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T05:08:38-07:00","id":683003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682799#post682799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, there is a certain monster-movie feel to them. Sure, they are tough, but if they run into an Anathema, they could get splatted. So, stick together, and with a lot of skill and a little luck, the PC Dragon-Bloods can triumph over a superior opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that hasn't worked so well in the past. Specifically, I've noticed a tendency by Celestials to kill Dragon-Blooded games by their mere presence that's made me feel the &quot;What Solar Exalted?&quot; section from the Storyteller section of Exalted: the Dragon-Blooded should've been in 2e where it was needed even more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T06:17:04-07:00","id":683048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682799#post682799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also really enjoy the experience of my PC somewhat hoodwinked. Most of the Immaculate Doctrine is bullshit, but hey, it tells my PC that he's enlightened and can do no wrong. Sounds like fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>Pedantry mode engaged: The Immaculate Philosophy does not say that DBs are morally perfect beings. It says that they are spiritually superior, such that the morally/karmically correct thing for a mortal to do is always &quot;obey the DB,&quot; but the DB can still be wrong or behave unjustly - it just sabotages their own enlightenment rather than that of the mortals who obey them. The Immaculate Philosophy has opinions about the just treatment of inferiors by their superiors and has enacted both peaceful and violent resistance against local rulers who grow too tyrannical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:22:47-07:00","id":683088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683048#post683048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pedantry mode engaged: The Immaculate Philosophy does not say that DBs are morally perfect beings. It says that they are spiritually superior, such that the morally/karmically correct thing for a mortal to do is always &quot;obey the DB,&quot; but the DB can still be wrong or behave unjustly - it just sabotages their own enlightenment rather than that of the mortals who obey them. The Immaculate Philosophy has opinions about the just treatment of inferiors by their superiors and has enacted both peaceful and violent resistance against local rulers who grow too tyrannical.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I think it might be interesting to play (or have a villain) a DB who thinks that, rather than it being actually true. Someone so narcissistic that they believe themselves to be beyond reproach, that their inherent enlightenment gives them carte-blanche to do whatever they want. Like Peleps Deled but with <i>even more </i>smug superiority.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Damn, my worry that I had misspelled Narcissistic and not being able to use my browser's spell check made me totally miss the spelling of carte-blanche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1982,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1982-spacepup","user":"Spacepup","date":". 09-30-2015, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1982-spacepup","name":"Spacepup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:30:26-07:00","id":683095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacepup</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683088#post683088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I think it might be interesting to play (or have a villain) a DB who thinks that, rather than it being actually true. Someone so narcissistic that they believe themselves to be beyond reproach, that their inherent enlightenment gives them cart-blanche to do whatever they want. Like Peleps Deled but with <i>even more </i>smug superiority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely! That's absolutely supported by the canon, that some of the Princes of the Earth believe that everything they do must be justified because they are Exalted. The dynamic between that person, the people who enable them, and the people who push back against them seems like it would be a lot of fun to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:03:23-07:00","id":683120,"title":"","content":"Man, now I'm thinking about about Immaculate uprisings against overly cruel rulers, and got to thinking about how cool it would be to have an Ikko Ikki situation somewhere one the isle. Where the Immaculate order had acted either officially or unofficially against some local governor who had gone too deep and come out the asshole end of enlightenment. And after the Immaculate order was done beating sense through the back of the offender's head they just kind of... never left; leaving some Realm regent to have some kind of 'Death, Taxes, and those warrior monks on Mt. Hiei&quot; kind of moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1982-spacepup","name":"Spacepup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:08:52-07:00","id":683132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacepup</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683120#post683120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some local governor who had gone too deep and come out the asshole end of enlightenment.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Asshole end of <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">enlightenment</span></span></span>&quot; is now one of my new favorite phases. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:22:35-07:00","id":683168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacepup</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683120#post683120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, now I'm thinking about about Immaculate uprisings against overly cruel rulers, and got to thinking about how cool it would be to have an Ikko Ikki situation somewhere one the isle. Where the Immaculate order had acted either officially or unofficially against some local governor who had gone too deep and come out the asshole end of enlightenment. And after the Immaculate order was done beating sense through the back of the offender's head they just kind of... never left; leaving some Realm regent to have some kind of 'Death, Taxes, and those warrior monks on Mt. Hiei&quot; kind of moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been toying with the idea of a satrap where that is just about to happen. Except, you know, it'll spiral out of control and end with the foundation of a New Realm/atrocity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:29:13-07:00","id":683178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682490#post682490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to see what Dragonblooded can do when they're not getting Worfed on anymore. Looking forward to What Fire Has Wrought.</div> </div> </div> </div>My preferred level of power for Terrestrials is &quot;Can take on <i>one</i> Celestial of the same Essence and win, but it's going to be quite difficult&quot;. And the strongest of them can even take on <i>two</i> Celestials but they'll have to push themselves to the limit. I don't like the whole &quot;a whole brotherhood gets shat on by one Celestial&quot; 2e has going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T09:09:33-07:00","id":683232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683178#post683178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My preferred level of power for Terrestrials is &quot;Can take on <i>one</i> Celestial of the same Essence and win, but it's going to be quite difficult&quot;. And the strongest of them can even take on <i>two</i> Celestials but they'll have to push themselves to the limit. I don't like the whole &quot;a whole brotherhood gets shat on by one Celestial&quot; 2e has going on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My ideal power levels for a Dragonblooded game:<br /> <br /> - Full Circle of Terrestrials vs a Celestial of equal power would be a toss up. Terrestrials might have a slight advantage, because there are more of them.<br /> - Full Circle of Terrestrials vs a Celestial of marginally greater power would have to think quick on their feet.<br /> - The bad ass two hundred year old Terrestrial who has survived centuries of shit thrown at them and unfortunately outlived the rest of his circle is a scary mofo. Celestial Exalts should be wary no matter what their power level. <br /> <br /> Not sure how I'd adjust the power levels for a Celestial game. Run as a Combat Unit? Maybe more to the tune of Frostnav's idea. Don't want the ST to have to keep track of 15 NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T09:27:44-07:00","id":683242,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a whole brotherhood should be able to take down a Solar (unless it's a very experienced Solar), that's why the Wyld Hunt is scary.<br /> <br /> This is also important because in your game, if you're running Solars, the Wyld Hunt isn't going to fight one, it's going to fight 5 at the same time. My preferred difficult for that is: the Solars most likely win, but it's not trivial and maybe the Dragonblood kill one Solar. Because the Wyld Hunt is a very serious threat (the kind that turns up once a story at most, unless your game is set in a Realm satrapy).<br /> <br /> Whereas in the last game, when I sent small Wyld Hunts twice to attack the PCs, near the beginning of the game when they had about 30xp, they completely wiped the floor with the Dragonblood.\u200b Which is why it only happened twice (after that, they'd killed most of the DBs in Greyfalls).<br /> <br /> (Maybe I should have inst\u200bead used the not-at-all likely, but entirely stereotypical, 5 Immaculates, each of whom has mastered one style).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-30-2015, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T09:50:03-07:00","id":683250,"title":"","content":"Huh. I guess I like my DB's a little more powerful than most people have them. I know they're not supposed to be as strong, but Terrestrials are still <i>Exalted</i>. Indeed the only real mechanical difference is their Charms--a DB with STR 5 Melee 5 and a Solar with STR 5 Melee 5, wielding the same weapon with no Charms, are going to do the same amount of damage. Of course Charms <b>are</b> a massive advantage for the Celestial (especially if they're a Solaroid). But I really like the idea of a crafty/incredibly skilled DB being able to hold their own anyway. They'll have to use every goddamn trick in the book, and will probably collapse in exhaustion at the end (which is why the Realm uses brotherhoods in the Wyld Hunt, to make things easier), but they could take on a Celestial single-handedly. I also like the idea of them using their weaker status as an advantage, making their Celestial opponent go &quot;Hah, this guy's just a Dragon-Blooded, this is gonna be so damn easy--wait what he's actually doing damage, shit, looks like I gotta actually care--oh fuck I'm getting beaten on by a fucking <i>Terrestrial</i> what the hell--&quot;. And then the Celestial overextends themselves, angry and hellbent on proving their superior status amongst the Exalted Host--only to fuck up that one critical moment and get a jade daiklaive to the chest. The bigger they are, the harder they fall, after all.<br /> <br /> Y'all already know I like my Exalted anime as hell, and few things are more anime than the scrappy underdog beating the much bigger guy. Even the mighty Goliath was slain by the humble David.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T10:53:29-07:00","id":683293,"title":"","content":"@OP, with the caveat that I'm taking &quot;don't turn this into a thread about how my conception of Solars is bad and wrong&quot; to mean &quot;don't long this thread out with a massive argument&quot; not &quot;just don't disagree with me at all&quot;...<br /> <br /> ... I don't see Solars as unironic heroes any more than Gilgamesh and Achilles and Conan. Ironic? Fuck no. They just aren't built in the direction of giving a damn about being ironic to goodness and light in the first place, so much as just being like questionable heroes from epics in the first place.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I love the duality of the Dragonblooded and Solars both being the scrappiest of the scrappy and the highest, given the keys to the kingdom and the crown upon their brow without having to fight for it, in different contexts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T11:06:52-07:00","id":683303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683250#post683250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I guess I like my DB's a little more powerful than most people have them. I know they're not supposed to be as strong, but Terrestrials are still <i>Exalted</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial Exalts are the &quot;Teamwork&quot; exalts. They work together to achieve higher goals. Themes of Blood is Thicker than Water, Friendship is Magic,and Betrayal of those values are scattered all through that splat.<br /> <br /> Most of the time, this works out great. In a Dragonblooded game, you have multiple players for a ready made Circle of Dragonbloods. In a Celestial Game, you going to throw multiple Dragonbloods at your players to deal with. In mixed games, this gets iffy, but not every Dragonblood is going to want to be with other Dragonbloods.<br /> <br /> But there is always the Golden Rule of Role Playing. If you want your Dragonbloods to be able to solo Solars at your gaming table, go for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T11:37:30-07:00","id":683346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683250#post683250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I really like the idea of a crafty/incredibly skilled DB being able to hold their own anyway. They'll have to use every goddamn trick in the book, [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I'd have with this is...<br /> ...who says the Solar hasn't read the same book?<br /> <br /> Basically, saying &quot;With enough determination, DBs can beat Solars&quot; sounds to me as if a Solar had a fixed power level which a DB can overcome if he just... spends enough willpower, or something. As if the Solar couldn't do the same. They're <i>both</i> fighting for their lives in this scenario, and once the Solar recognises the DB as actual threat, he can be just as determined to survive.<br /> Also, I <i>immensely dislike</i> definite outcomes.<br /> <br /> Which is why I imagine [a one on one fight] as a &quot;One in X&quot; chance for a DB to win, with X being a rather large number. (At least 8, I guess.) The difference is, there are (metaphorically) ten thousand dragons, and only three hundred Solar(oid)s. Adding in the (3ed) 400 Lunars makes 700 Celestials (assuming the Sids stay in the background). Assuming the &quot;10 thousand&quot; number is anywhere near the truth, that makes a bit more than 14 DB per Celestial. So, even in consecutive 1-on-1 battles of DB vs. Celestial, the DBs could have an advantage. Add in that their powers work better the larger their groups are, and... well, luckily, they aren't one large group, and you're probably going to have a few on your side after a while.<br /> <br /> But until then, don't go into open warfare. They have reserves. You might be able to kill this one, and the next, and the one after that, but <i>one</i> day, you will slip. You can't kill all of them, and they only have to kill the one of you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, once you get to groups, all bets are off, and it starts to depend on group synergy and teamwork.<br /> And DBs have a strong tendency to be good at teamwork and synergy. Heck, if I remember correctly, they had a charm that allowed them to instantly form an intimacy to a group of allies, allowing even usually mortal enemies to fight together like brothers against a common enemy.<br /> (Edit: Looked it up. &quot;Unflagging Vengeance Meditation&quot;, MoEP: DB, page 144. You instantly form an intimacy towards a goal, and [your Essence] other characters can join you. If anyone abandons the goal prematurely, they suffer [Essence of all characters together] lethal damage.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":7262,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","user":"Amakawa Yuuto","date":". 09-30-2015, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T12:30:00-07:00","id":683432,"title":"","content":"The &quot;how many DBs does it take to kill a Solar&quot; discussion doesn't seem like it has much of a point to me. It just falls into the common traps all &quot;versus&quot; discussions tend to. &quot;Can defeat&quot; doesn't mean &quot;will defeat&quot;. A lone Dragon-Blood should be able to kill a lone Solar, but a lone mortal is capable of killing a Solar as well - it all depends on who each person is, what they do and what happens around them. Being a Solar is an advantage when compared to a Dragon-Blooded, but that's not the only advantage to be had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T13:02:36-07:00","id":683451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683432#post683432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &amp;quot;how many DBs does it take to kill a Solar&amp;quot; discussion doesn't seem like it has much of a point to me. It just falls into the common traps all &amp;quot;versus&amp;quot; discussions tend to. &amp;quot;Can defeat&amp;quot; doesn't mean &amp;quot;will defeat&amp;quot;. A lone Dragon-Blood should be able to kill a lone Solar, but a lone mortal is capable of killing a Solar as well - it all depends on who each person is, what they do and what happens around them. Being a Solar is an advantage when compared to a Dragon-Blooded, but that's not the only advantage to be had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. If a sworn brotherhood attacked a dawn or a righty zenith or something they're probably not going to make it. On the other hand if they sneak attack a twilight doctor they might not even lose one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T13:06:32-07:00","id":683455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683451#post683451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much this. If a sworn brotherhood attacked a dawn or a righty zenith or something they're probably not going to make it. On the other hand if they sneak attack a twilight doctor they might not even lose one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, even Panther was apparently once held captive by what appears to be an ordinary mortal woman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T13:14:02-07:00","id":683457,"title":"","content":"Invincible Sword Princess is probably going to defeat any comparable foe in a 1 on 1 fight. But I mean, come on, she's <i>Invincible Sword Princess</i> and defeating powerful enemies is what she was specifically built to do. The other 149 Solars are <i>not</i> Invincible Sword Princess, and could easily find themselves defeated by a foe that Invincible Sword Princess would have been capable of defeating.<br /> <br /> That is one of the biggest problems in &quot;vs&quot; discussions in Exalted - many people seem to default to the idea that every Solar is optimized Invincible Sword Princess. Even if Invincible Sword Princess was capable of defeating Imminent Thunder in a duel, that doesn't mean that <i>any</i> Solar could defeat him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T14:35:56-07:00","id":683559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">even Panther was apparently once held captive by what appears to be an ordinary mortal woman.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I imagine there have been a lot of people who would be surprised to find they actually made fighter characters who weren't really equipped to escape bonds or prisons, or would be kind of helpless if an enemy broke all of their hands and legs. There are some kinds of people who do recognise these definciencies and look upon them with abject horror, feeling a need to cover every possible weakness as a defence against gleeful STs who are just waiting for them to fall asleep so they can send a death squad past their lack of anti-surprise Charms, but I think they're kind of weird. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a sworn brotherhood attacked a dawn or a righty zenith or something they're probably not going to make it.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;A&quot; Dawn? What is &quot;a&quot; Dawn? Are there not immense numbers of variations on what a Dawn is? Are there not, for instance, Dawns who haven't yet or never will invest in Charms to effectively give them defense in every direction, meaning that they can be flanked fairly easily? Describe this lone Dawn who is probably fighting off a Sworn Brotherhood in more detail, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T14:51:21-07:00","id":683566,"title":"","content":"A Dawn Caste can also be a peerless tactician and statesman, who is nonetheless not significantly tougher in personal combat than their mortal soldiers. So to talk about a &quot;sworn brotherhood attacking a Dawn&quot; is effectively about as meaningful as a &quot;ninja versus Viking&quot; argument. Even if we <i>do </i>define that Dawn Caste Solar and the five Dragon-Blooded who oppose them, there's still only so much information a white-room comparison is going to give us. Not unless we say why they're fighting, where they meet, what they want and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:15:21-07:00","id":683586,"title":"","content":"Darn it, every time I see this thread title, I get the song from Office Space stuck in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T16:15:59-07:00","id":683630,"title":"","content":"It <i>does</i> feel good to be a Dynast. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T18:36:01-07:00","id":683694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683559#post683559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there not immense numbers of variations on what a Dawn is? Are there not, for instance, Dawns who haven't yet or never will invest in Charms to effectively give them defense in every direction, meaning that they can be flanked fairly easily? Describe this lone Dawn who is probably fighting off a Sworn Brotherhood in more detail, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>THANK YOU. <br /> <br /> Categorical statements like &quot;they cannot defeat A Dawn who will just kick them apart&quot; just drive me nuts. I look forward to playing a Dawn in 3e who is maybe OK at actual PAWNCHing but goddamn amazing at just pissing enemies off by being unhittable/unhurtable/messing up their ability to fight effectively without actually being all that good at <i>hurting</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T19:23:34-07:00","id":683754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683559#post683559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are there not immense numbers of variations on what a Dawn is? Are there not, for instance, Dawns who haven't yet or never will invest in Charms to effectively give them defense in every direction, meaning that they can be flanked fairly easily? Describe this lone Dawn who is probably fighting off a Sworn Brotherhood in more detail, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I DID say they only probably won't make it, the possibility is there, but dawn caste Solars were chosen by the sun for their peerless martial prowess. Obviously ones who focus on being able to thread an arrow through a helmets eye hole at 200 yards or the ones who unleash a cascade of 1,000 knives carried on the wind probably won't be ready in eight directions, but they're really hard to fight for other reasons. The archer for example will probably have two or three of them dead before they even close to close range, if they get there at all. Even brawl and tiger style, which we've been told is more for the single target death thing wouldn't be so bad, as each one you take out takes out a good chunk of their threat. Especially if DBs have a lot of synergy going on, quickly dismantling them is a big bonus. They are, in combat anyway, the most dangerous of the exalted host, bar none. <br /> <br /> Zel's dawn might actually be even better at fighting a brotherhood of DBs because the first rule of fighting multiple opponents is don't get hit/hurt because you're in it for the long haul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T19:40:08-07:00","id":683761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683586#post683586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darn it, every time I see this thread title, I get the song from Office Space stuck in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>What song is that?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking it's not the one they play when they take apart the copy machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T22:04:42-07:00","id":683942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682617#post682617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what degree do you think the game should emphasize that the Realm is squatting on the ruins of a bigger empire the Host is physically incapable of operating or maintaining, like Kevin trying to stay at home after his parents forget him at home (but probably less insulting than that comparison)?</div> </div> </div> </div>So I've had this idea floating around in my head for awhile, trying to differentiate some of the basic differences between the High First Age, the Shogunate and the Second Age. <br /> <br /> Basically in the High First Age, the Solar Deliberative protected the people and built its infrastructure through powerful artifacts, which could control the weather, help move goods vast distances, ensure that crops would grow well, etc. But, importantly, they also had powerful ties and oaths to the spirits, and these helped to improve the quality of life for the the people of the First Age. <br /> <br /> When the Usurpation occurred and the Shogunate arose, many of the old contracts with the spirit courts were broken. No longer could farmers rely on the small gods to bring rain on time or fertilize their crops. Suddenly rivers would flood, and natural disasters (once almost unheard of in the First Age) were comparatively commonplace. This mattered little to the Dragon Blooded though. Even with the loss of the spirits assistance, the artifacts and wonders of the Solar Exalted proved capable of ensuring that there was enough food to eat, that the mines continued to provide ore, and that while the quality of life for the average farmer and worker was quite a bit worse than it was in the First Age, for many people (especially in the cities) there was almost no change whatsoever. <br /> <br /> When the Contagion hit, and then the subsequent Balorian Crusade arrived, many of those ancient artifacts were largely destroyed or rendered useless.<br /> <br /> So the Dragon Blooded of the Realm turned to the spirits to ensure that the quality of their life would continue as it always did. Through bribery and outright bullying, the Dragon Blooded forced spirits to begin providing their blessings to the people of the Realm. Road spirits bless the caravans of Realm merchants to move quickly along their roads. Field gods bless the land so that farmers can produce more than they would otherwise be able to. Salt gods are made to produce plenty of salt for the Realm to mine. What this means is that the quality of life for Dragon Blooded and many of the nobles in the Realm is essentially no different than it was for Dragon Blooded and the wealthy in the Shogunate. It's just that, instead of getting that lifestyle through the use of artifacts (like the Shogunate did), they do so through the blessings of the gods and elementals. <br /> <br /> In such a case, the artifacts of the First Age are interesting and useful, but not exactly vital. As of Year Zero the Realm's economy, growth and existence is largely based around the activities of spirits, who have been bribed, bullied or cajoled, rather than the ancient magics of the First Age. In fact, if you were to remove every First Age and Shogunate era artifact from the Realm (with the exception of the Defense Grid) you wouldn't see much of a difference in the lives of the commoners, the middle classes, the nobles or the Dragon Blooded. In contrast Lookshy (true to its Shogunate roots) relies heavily on the ancient First Age artifacts and would implode if it no longer had such things.<br /> <br /> This helps to set the Realm up as an empire that has its own sense of self and whose existence and means of power are distinct from both the Shogunate and the world of the High First Age. To go your example, sort of like Kevin from Home Alone, rather than living in his parents house, instead building his own massive tree house that has running water, and a TV he can operate by plugging it into the lemons that grow on the tree. <br /> <br /> While probably not as comfortable as his parents house, it would still pretty impressive and not necessarily something that people would look down on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T01:26:28-07:00","id":684083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683250#post683250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Everything you've said.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This guy.<br /> <br /> I like this guy.<br /> <br /> I agree with you, and its something i've spouted for as long as I can remember on these forums. The Dragon-Blooded are Exalted, capital E, and badass. Even for a Solar, facing down one of the Terrestrials is going to be a frightening experience. The Solar is going to have to be wary and keep up his guard, because he's dealing with one of <i>the most powerful and skilled beings in Creation</i>. Especially in a situation where they are both trained warriors and soldiers. Sure, the Solar has more metaphysical oomph, and the Dragon-Blood should know he's fighting for his life, and is going to have to work hard and really use all advantages available to him, but it should never be a clear outcome between two roughly equal experienced combatants.<br /> <br /> That said, White Room scenario, a Solar is likely going to win. Not 100%, of course, but its more likely. A Dragon-Blood should not try to face a Solar on his terms. A Solar is defined by perfection and peerless skill, so you don't really want to engage on a level playing field unless you absolutely have to. Gotta use them brains and tactics, lure the Solar into a trap, get him pissed enough to waste Essence if you can, have a mortal soldier help you from surprise (the more pious the better).<br /> <br /> Used to, when Dragon-Bloods had Free Reflexives, if you could determine whether the Anathema you were fighting had any Combos or not, you could face them down pretty easily. Get them to attack you with a Charm, and they were left wide open. The good ole days....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T02:16:22-07:00","id":684104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683048#post683048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pedantry mode engaged: The Immaculate Philosophy does not say that DBs are morally perfect beings. It says that they are spiritually superior, such that the morally/karmically correct thing for a mortal to do is always &quot;obey the DB,&quot; but the DB can still be wrong or behave unjustly - it just sabotages their own enlightenment rather than that of the mortals who obey them. The Immaculate Philosophy has opinions about the just treatment of inferiors by their superiors and has enacted both peaceful and violent resistance against local rulers who grow too tyrannical.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;pedant&gt;<br /> We are talking about a faith that was tailor-made to justify mass enslavement (including the use of slaves purely for entertainment), wars of aggression and conquest, institutionalized theft, religious persecution, and mass murder. Oh, and it's a protection racket.<br /> <br /> If my faith tells me I can do all those things, and actually be in the <i>right</i>, well Hell, what IS wrong? <br /> &lt;/pendant&gt;<br /> <br /> The notion that a combat-specialized, equipped Solar could reasonably lose to a similarly outfitted and experienced Dragon-Blood in a fair fight takes the setting out back and shoots it. It's just not viable.<br /> The notion that all Solars are combat-specced is equally absurd. Arianna is not beating Avaku, period.<br /> Finally, since when did one Exalt beating up another one become the sole, or even the most important, distinction of their importance or narrative relevance?<br /> <br /> The Solar has reason to fear because the Dragon-Blood represents the tip of a very sharp and very large spear. If he doesn't kill that Dragon-Blood, he can bet his Caste Mark he will be hounded for weeks, months or years, and he stands a good chance of dying.<br /> <br /> And the Dragon-Blood shouldn't really be afraid of the Solar on this own. He can find his friends, get help from the local temple, and lead a Wyld Hunt. No, the danger isn't in the Solar now, it's the danger if the Solar is allowed to live for ten years, found a kingdom, raise an army, and come back.<br /> <br /> If you want the experience of being the biggest badass on the battlefield, then you want to be a Solar. If you want the experience of being a pretty big badass, and having an enormous empire and extended family of thousands of badasses backing you up, be a Dragon-Blood. Both are great experiences, which I enjoy. But the game doesn't by default validate all types of play for all Exalts. That would lead to narrative and mechanical mush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T02:46:18-07:00","id":684122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683754#post683754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I DID say they only probably won't make it, the possibility is there, but dawn caste Solars were chosen by the sun for their peerless martial prowess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, do you want me to build a Dawn Caste character who doesn't have more than three in any combat Ability? I can come up with dozens.<br /> <br /> Dear Glob is this an image of Dawns that excludes something as elementary as every single Jackie Chan character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The archer for example will probably have two or three of them dead before they even close to close range, if they get there at all. Even brawl and tiger style, which we've been told is more for the single target death thing wouldn't be so bad, as each one you take out takes out a good chunk of their threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your ideas are horrifying to me and I wish to immolate your newsletter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T02:47:21-07:00","id":684125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=683761#post683761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What song is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The one that plays over the montage of him slacking off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T02:59:22-07:00","id":684136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=684104#post684104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are talking about a faith that was tailor-made to justify mass enslavement (including the use of slaves purely for entertainment), wars of aggression and conquest, institutionalized theft, religious persecution, and mass murder. Oh, and it's a protection racket.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was tailor-made to justify Terrestrial rule, control unruly gods, and keep the Anathema in check. The rest is just the culture of the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T03:42:11-07:00","id":684197,"title":"","content":"I question the usefulness of the term &quot;fair fight&quot; when talking about combat between divinely-endowed heroes, one of whom is likely religiously motivated to defeat the other at all costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:15:22-07:00","id":684244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=684136#post684136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was tailor-made to justify Terrestrial rule, control unruly gods, and keep the Anathema in check. The rest is just the culture of the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it justifies that rule by force. Immaculate doctrine doesn't say &quot;Dragon-Bloods should be your rulers, but they will sit quietly on their Blessed Isle until you accept them.&quot; It says &quot;The Dragon-Blooded are the rightful rulers of Creation. If you disagree with this, and want to rule yourselves, or not give them your property, they can kill you.&quot; It may not literally say &quot;they have the right to kill you,&quot; but it doesn't NEED to, in much the same way that laws in Russia that outlaw &quot;gay propaganda,&quot; don't need to say &quot;we hate and want to oppress gays.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was redesigned to justify all of this, because Kejak cut a deal with Her Redness to use his Immaculate Order to help her assume control of all Creation, and keep the Wyld Hunt going. She gets to run an expansionist empire, and the Immaculate Order will hold her up as the rightful ruler of Creation, and justify her acts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T10:10:29-07:00","id":684592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=682412#post682412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly one of my biggest disappointments with the first two editions was that we didn't get nearly enough juicy details about the Great Houses. I really felt we could have used a Great Houses of the Realm book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit we don't have the awesome slogans of the Game of Thrones Houses or the various title shifting and favor trading that comes with real legislative power of House of Cards. <br /> <br /> We do have an elemental Aspect for most Great Houses. We have a short write-up of plans and members in the 2e hardback. Many members and their sub-plots show up in the Blessed Isle Compass. Many of the Dynastic Terrestrials of the Aspect books spend pages describing their relationship to their Great House. Also the &quot;Words not their own&quot; sections typically have other members of the Great House talking about how the Dynastic characters tie in to the overall scheme.<br /> <br /> That said, you have my support for a &quot;Great Houses of The Realm - Scarlet's Dynasty&quot; book. I would eat that up just as fast as a Shogunate supplement. <br /> <br /> I agree with the OP - Dragon-Blooded games are great games. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T18:11:28-07:00","id":685107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=684122#post684122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, do you want me to build a Dawn Caste character who doesn't have more than three in any combat Ability? I can come up with dozens.<br /> <br /> Dear Glob is this an image of Dawns that excludes something as elementary as every single Jackie Chan character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are also dozens of character concepts for zenith's and eclipses with almost nothing in their social stats, or twilights with almost nothing in mental stats. That still doesn't stop there from being certain roles and qualities that castes look for to exalt and enhance. In what way does Jackie Chan not fit the image of a Dawn, as presented in their second ed core spread? Except for that Jackie Chan is rarely shown to be able to throw enemies through solid stone pillars or anything like that. Is it because he doesn't fight multiple people at once or something? Because he does all the time. Is it because he can fight kind of silly sometimes? Because I think that just means he's a master of Orgiastic Fugative Style, he still ends up kicking everyone's ass anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=684122#post684122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your ideas are horrifying to me and I wish to immolate your newsletter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally blanking on the newsletter reference.<br /> <br /> <br /> Look, I think DBs are really cool, but part of what makes them cool is their weakness. We're comparing the very top of the exalted warriors to the very bottom. Wyld Hunts fail and die, sometimes they don't, but post empress/jade prison they've been doing it a lot more. When they die to Twilights it's probably because of some powerful sorcery or long ago activated artiface or engineered plague or something, when they die to nights it's probably because they got seriously out maneuvered and assassinated, and when they die to Dawns it's probably because they got their cushioned behinds handed to them in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T18:28:29-07:00","id":685120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685107#post685107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm totally blanking on the newsletter reference.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wlMwc1c0HRQ\" data-code=\"wlMwc1c0HRQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wlMwc1c0HRQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T18:37:07-07:00","id":685125,"title":"","content":"Monkey, three dots is far from &quot;almost nothing.&quot; It's literally more than half the distance you <i>can</i> even go. <i>2 dots</i> is the threshold for &quot;I do this shit for a living.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you lump together 100 random guys with dots in a given Ability, the top guy? He's almost certainly a 3. If you want to <i>guarantee</i> finding someone with a 5 you'll want to expand your sample size to probably about a million.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-01-2015, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T18:56:41-07:00","id":685134,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem is the math of character generation.<br /> <br /> I try to make organic characters that feel like 'new-kid-on-the-block' heroes. At the same time, it's really hard not to kick an attribute or ability to four or five if I know that it's going to be important to my character's utility and ability to survive. Especially once you realize that if you don't do it now, it means having to sink more XP into it later.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T21:24:01-07:00","id":685254,"title":"","content":"I agree. I like playing that too, because I want to develop the character.<br /> <br /> Generally, making a Solar, I think &quot;I want him to be, say, an excellent swordsman. So I'll give him Melee 4 and some Melee charms, and 2 or 3 in everything else.&quot;<br /> <br /> But, because of the BP/XP system, that's a terrible way to do it. He should have Melee 5 (+3 spec), and also 3 or 4 other abilities at 5. And Str 3/Dex 5/Sta 3. Well, Str 2/Dex 5/Sta 4, preferably, then buy Str 3 in-game.<br /> <br /> I kind of want to build up my stats to high levels in play, but the system discourages that.<br /> <br /> I guess the idea is that your skill comes from your charms, but because mortals don't have charms, a Solar with Melee 5 is as good (in 3rd ed, much better, because of his free excellency) as the greatest duelling master in the world, so I find that awkward to wrap my head around.<br /> <br /> <br /> I currently play a No Moo\u200bn Sorcerer/shapeshifter, and I honestly find it bizarre how huge a lot of his stats are. I don't really consider him to be, say, a master of manipulation, better at kung-fu than any mortal, better at speeches or playing instruments than almost anyone, but technically he is. It's kind of weird. I think I'll strip back a lot of his stats when I convert to 3rd ed and buy more spells instead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-02-2015, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T22:06:53-07:00","id":685281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685125#post685125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monkey, three dots is far from &quot;almost nothing.&quot; It's literally more than half the distance you <i>can</i> even go. <i>2 dots</i> is the threshold for &quot;I do this shit for a living.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you lump together 100 random guys with dots in a given Ability, the top guy? He's almost certainly a 3. If you want to <i>guarantee</i> finding someone with a 5 you'll want to expand your sample size to probably about a million.</div> </div> </div> </div>aye, heroic mortals by themselves are already probably one in a million- they not only have a 3 they have 3's in multiple abilities, and the ones that become Solar usually have a 5 in one. you can't think small with this kind of thing when it comes to Exalted: even if your mortal, your making someone who has led a rare and interesting life. sure even the lowest farmhand or slave can become a Solar, but heroic mortals have usually done far more than that. they have more bonus points than anyone after all.<br /> <br /> I mean, most people in Creation never even see an Exalt in their life. to be a Dragon-Blooded is to be one of the 1% in all of Creation and own more wealth and power by the mere dint of your status than most can dream of, to be a Celestial Exalt is to belong to clubs that are more fewer in number and more exclusive than being a nation's representative in the United Nations and chosen by less fair means. To be a heroic mortal is to be not some random schmuck who got lucky, but one who has worked hard for years to get to the position they are now, who achieved what they have achieved through pure sweat, blood and tears when most mortals would've quit a long time ago- less some random person, and more like the local celebrity whose talents were recognized and got a better life going for him because of them the thing is about ability? people can see when someone has talent or skill, people recognize it when someone is good at something, and they value being able to have that. it took a while for me to figure this out, but a heroic mortal isn't living in a vacuum, they're living in a world where the skills they've developed are valued and encouraged because of how needed those skills are. a heroic mortal, I think shouldn't be just a soldier, they should be a captain or a champion of the ruler they fight for, because people recognize when a guy is good at swordplay and put him in a position to best use his sword see? even a heroic mortal isn't going zero-to-hero, because they're already a HEROIC mortal, they already went through that, if they were zero, they'd just be plain mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T22:15:44-07:00","id":685290,"title":"","content":"I think we should also point out a difference between abilities and attributes.<br /> <br /> I mean, 2 is an average attribute for a mortal, but a decent ability: something they've probably trained at. 1 is an average ability.<br /> <br /> This sort of implies that, if having a 5 in an attribute is as good as having a 5 in an ability, it must require a lot more work (as you start higher up) and of course, it does in terms of XP (since they're twice as hard to raise).<br /> <br /> In fact, the xp required to get from str 2 to str 5 is 36, to get from Athletics 0 to 5 is only 23.<br /> <br /> Uh, I'm not really sure where I'm going with this, but I feel it's somehow significant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T22:30:41-07:00","id":685294,"title":"","content":"Some more musing...<br /> <br /> Let's take me. I'm a teacher, got a Masters, etc. Let's be kind and say I have Intelligence 3 and 2 in everything else, Lore 3 from my MA, and... yeah, I'm not really that good at anything else. 0 or 1 in other abilities, maybe 2 in one or two of them. So let's say I have an average of 1 in each ability, that's 25 (perhaps that's a little generous).<br /> <br /> A starting Solar, before freebies has slightly more ability dots than me (3 more), but not much more.<br /> <br /> Let's say he's the thickest in his circle, he's mental tertiary... he's still as clever as me. Only much more charismatic, stronger, faster, tougher, better looking. He's just amazing.<br /> <br /> It's kind odd that he has only slightly more abilities than me, but far more attributes (he's not a Lunar).<br /> <br /> Presumably though, he then spend his freebies on favoured abilities and suddenly he has 5-ish abilities that he is literally one of the greatest mortals in the world at.<br /> Or he spends it on attributes and... isn't much more skilled than me? But still physically amazing, and super charismatic?<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not sure where I'm going with this, I'm just trying to put things in context.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T22:36:37-07:00","id":685295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685294#post685294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some more musing...<br /> <br /> Let's take me. I'm a teacher, got a Masters, etc. Let's be kind and say I have Intelligence 3 and 2 in everything else, Lore 3 from my MA, and... yeah, I'm not really that good at anything else. 0 or 1 in other abilities, maybe 2 in one or two of them. So let's say I have an average of 1 in each ability, that's 25 (perhaps that's a little generous).</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of people will not have one in each ability. You may have one in each ability that relates to daily living in a modern world, but human ability is a bit wider than that.<br /> <br /> Can you fly a plane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T22:51:05-07:00","id":685302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685125#post685125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monkey, three dots is far from &quot;almost nothing.&quot; It's literally more than half the distance you <i>can</i> even go. <i>2 dots</i> is the threshold for &quot;I do this shit for a living.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you lump together 100 random guys with dots in a given Ability, the top guy? He's almost certainly a 3. If you want to <i>guarantee</i> finding someone with a 5 you'll want to expand your sample size to probably about a million.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, sorry, that was my fault. I was going in completely the opposite direction and saying that there certainly exist Dawn character concepts with 3 dots in combat abilities, there even exists dawn character concepts with 2, or 1, or even zero*! They're sure as hell not the majority though, and even with three in a combat ability Solar charms make a huge, huge difference. I don't want to get too mechanical here but a Solar with 3 melee has access to Hungry Tiger, Fire and Stones, Dipping Swallow, Bulwark Stance, One Weapon Two Blows and Peony Blossom Attack, Call the Blade, Summoning the Loyal Steel and Iron Raptor Technique. A DB with 3 melee has access to Blinding Spark, Dragon Graced Weapon and Ghost Fire Blade.<br /> <br /> If any given Dawn Caste isn't likely to have 5 in their combat stat, any given DB isn't either.<br /> <br /> <br /> *For instance a student whom a master sees a single flash of ultimate innate talent and decides to teach them everything about swordplay, or a master archer who, through some accident, has forgotten all he once knew about archery, but vows to one day because that legend again, ect. There's a tone of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T22:57:45-07:00","id":685304,"title":"","content":"A fair point.<br /> <br /> As I said, I'm not sure where I'm going with this, just trying to expound what abilities are precisely.<br /> <br /> So, I guess that reinforces Alucard's point: that most people will have, say 1 ability at 2 (the thing they do most of the time), and I guess maybe another 10 dots at 1, perhaps, and that's it. So perhaps a master cooper has Craft (Barrel) 3, and a journeyman has 2.<br /> But you're very unlikely to find anyone with Craft (Barrel) 4 in a town, and definitely not 5.<br /> <br /> Which makes Solars (a lot of whom have, after being exalted for a couple of months, 4 or 5 abilities at 5) amazing (DBs too).<br /> <br /> <br /> I find this awkward in a certain way. Not awkward in the sense that I don't want my Solar to start with an ability at 5. That's fine. Say I'm playing a swordsman (I'm choosing this because it's an incredibly stereotypical example), taking Melee 5 is probably fine.<br /> The weird bit is that character generation also wants me to take a bunch of other abilities at 5 too. So I take Dodge 5, because I probably dodge around in combat. And then I take Athletics 5, because I guess I do a lot of exercise? And then I take Ride 5, because sure I ride a horse... and at this point I'm just looking for excuses because I need something to put these 5s into.<br /> <br /> I guess really, as a master swordsman, it'd probably be better to spend these freebies on having Str/Dex 5 and Sta 4, (12 freebies, plus Melee 5 +2 swords for the other 3) but it's a little suboptimal (and Solar magic is ability based). so the game kind of discourages me from doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T23:22:07-07:00","id":685322,"title":"","content":"With DBs it's not quite as bad, since your concept will invariably include going to the best schools in the world anyway, so if your Tepet Swordsman (I know swordsman is a boring concept, I'm just using it as an example because it's easy) has Lore 5, War 5, Melee 5, Linguistics 5 and Dodge 5, it's not all that out of place.<br /> <br /> What I actually found myself doing with DBs, was taking an absolute ton of favoured specialities (you get the second-best rate of XP/BP return on them, and they're used in DB excellencies anyway). \u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T23:26:32-07:00","id":685323,"title":"","content":"With DBs, it's not as bad, because you probably went to one of the world's best schools anyway, so if your Tepet swordsman also has War 5, Lore 5 and Linguistics 5, it's not that out of place.<br /> <br /> Plus, because specialities count for DB excellencies, I tended to buy a lot of them (you get a 6xp per bp rate of return), so that meant the character was more specialised, rather than really good at tons of stuff that didn't really come from the character.<br /> <br /> My first Solar was amazing at loads of stuff his background gave little justification for, which made the other players tease me a lot about how I must have had an amazing library in my Yurt and a martial artist living next door.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T23:29:12-07:00","id":685324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685302#post685302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, sorry, that was my fault. I was going in completely the opposite direction and saying that there certainly exist Dawn character concepts with 3 dots in combat abilities, there even exists dawn character concepts with 2, or 1, or even zero*! They're sure as hell not the majority though, and even with three in a combat ability Solar charms make a huge, huge difference. I don't want to get too mechanical here but a Solar with 3 melee has access to Hungry Tiger, Fire and Stones, Dipping Swallow, Bulwark Stance, One Weapon Two Blows and Peony Blossom Attack, Call the Blade, Summoning the Loyal Steel and Iron Raptor Technique. A DB with 3 melee has access to Blinding Spark, Dragon Graced Weapon and Ghost Fire Blade.<br /> <br /> If any given Dawn Caste isn't likely to have 5 in their combat stat, any given DB isn't either.<br /> <br /> <br /> *For instance a student whom a master sees a single flash of ultimate innate talent and decides to teach them everything about swordplay, or a master archer who, through some accident, has forgotten all he once knew about archery, but vows to one day because that legend again, ect. There's a tone of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of want to play a Dawn with Int 5, War 5 and no combat dots (because he's a chess or gateway prodigy) who then finds that his Dawn exaltation makes learning combat really easy, and over the course of the game develops into a mighty swordsman, even though he grew up as, say, a cobbler or something.<br /> <br /> Or, for that matter, any Dawn from a non-combat background who learns from a kung-fu master during the game on his quest to become a hero (because it's an important part of the hero's journey), but I guess he ought to be good at something Dawn-esque to get Dawn exaltation in the first place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T00:15:11-07:00","id":685333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685302#post685302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, sorry, that was my fault. I was going in completely the opposite direction and saying that there certainly exist Dawn character concepts with 3 dots in combat abilities, there even exists dawn character concepts with 2, or 1, or even zero*! They're sure as hell not the majority though, and even with three in a combat ability Solar charms make a huge, huge difference. I don't want to get too mechanical here but a Solar with 3 melee has access to Hungry Tiger, Fire and Stones, Dipping Swallow, Bulwark Stance, One Weapon Two Blows and Peony Blossom Attack, Call the Blade, Summoning the Loyal Steel and Iron Raptor Technique. A DB with 3 melee has access to Blinding Spark, Dragon Graced Weapon and Ghost Fire Blade.</div> </div> </div> </div>You literally compared one of the most bloated Ability Charm trees of one of the most Charm-bloated Exalt types in the entire gameline with a splat who got exactly one supplement in the entire run of Ex2.<br /> <br /> Try comparing Solar Stealth instead.<br /> <br /> We've been told, IIRC, that other splats will have more robust Charm trees in Ex3, so hopefully this isn't an argument next edition.<br /> <br /> Raziere: this is another reason I hope &quot;heroic&quot; as a designation is going out the window.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T00:26:42-07:00","id":685336,"title":"","content":"Or Solar awareness.<br /> <br /> Actually, most Night charms were pretty thin on the ground.<br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of &quot;heroic&quot; mortals vs &quot;non-heroic&quot; mortals, I suspect that will be gone, because of replacing Extras with Battle Groups. I suspect it'll just be mortals, though in terms of character gen, if you play a mortal, it'll probably assume you're more skilled than the average peasant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T00:45:42-07:00","id":685339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685333#post685333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You literally compared one of the most bloated Ability Charm trees of one of the most Charm-bloated Exalt types in the entire gameline with a splat who got exactly one supplement in the entire run of Ex2.<br /> <br /> Try comparing Solar Stealth instead.<br /> <br /> We've been told, IIRC, that other splats will have more robust Charm trees in Ex3, so hopefully this isn't an argument next edition.<br /> <br /> Raziere: this is another reason I hope &quot;heroic&quot; as a designation is going out the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, granted. We were talking about dawn warriors vs Wyld Hunt though, so melee was my natural go-to. Even comparing stealth though, with Solar's 2 charms to DBs 5, the Solar has two perfect stealth effects. DBs on the other hand get silent actions, or trackless passage (Assuming no essence users are doing the tracking). The raw, straightforward power of Solar charms almost can't be overstated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T01:04:29-07:00","id":685351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685333#post685333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raziere: this is another reason I hope &quot;heroic&quot; as a designation is going out the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>....<i>why?</i> it only when I figured out how that designation meant, that I was able to create good Solar concepts at all. some people are better at creating Solars from heroic mortals, some are better at creating them from normal ones, get over it. its a good thing in my opinion. sure Exaltation doesn't distinguish between the guy who is only a farmhand and the guy who successfully becomes a merchant prince, but that doesn't mean everyone can make a character from a complete zero, from someone completely normal. I never saw it as a metaphysical difference or whatever, its just the difference between one guy who gone out and did stuff story-wise and one who kept living a normal life, if they both Exalt as a Solar, who cares?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6018,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","user":"Raziere","date":". 10-02-2015, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T01:08:45-07:00","id":685352,"title":"","content":"If only &quot;heroic&quot; (read: &quot;characters built <i>like this</i>&quot;) mortals can Exalt, Raziere, the Solar Exaltation <i>would</i> favor the merchant prince over the serf working the subsistence farm. The merchant prince has avenues for learning a broad number of skills, becoming well-traveled, et cetera. <br /> <br /> The Sun uplifts heroes, but heroes don't need to be a special character class for mortal PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-02-2015, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T01:19:52-07:00","id":685354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685352#post685352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If only &quot;heroic&quot; mortals can Exalt, Raziere, the Solar Exaltation <i>would</i> favor the merchant prince over the serf working the subsistence farm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never saw it as a metaphysical difference, only a story one. so if your going to argue against me based on some stupidity some other person spat out about the Loom of Fate or whatever, save it. my preference is purely because I don't find any normal mortal interesting enough for a story, that is all, and furthermore do not care for whatever &quot;the power is in all of humanity&quot; lessons or &quot;Exaltation is the random chance of Exalting anyone&quot; you care to teach me, I'm sure I heard them all before and found them eye-rolling.<br /> <br /> the only difference between one or the other is that one mortal did more stuff than the other, which has no impact on Exaltation, not really. I mean can you blame me if I cannot relate to or desire to play as an iron age farmhand whose greatest achievement in life is growing successful crops this year?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T01:50:07-07:00","id":685360,"title":"","content":"Maybe the issue is heroic is so subjective.<br /> <br /> I was going to make a point about King David being an iron-age shepherd who exalts fighting Goliath even though he's had no weapons training, and then becomes a great general, soldier, etc (which have nothing to do with the skills he learnt as a kid). But then I realised we'd argue about whether he was &quot;heroic&quot; in the first place.<br /> <br /> So it's probably easier just to drop it.<br /> <br /> I do think Raziere is probably right about it being more of a story difference (ie who is and isn't an extra) rather than a metaphysical one, but sometimes writers forgot that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T02:23:09-07:00","id":685380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685107#post685107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what way does Jackie Chan not fit the image of a Dawn, as presented in their second ed core spread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jackie Chan characters are the protagonists of his films.<br /> <br /> In very few of his old school Chinese films is he portrayed as the greatest martial artist in his setting, yet he still possesses a certain je ne sais quo that carries him through to impressive and improbable victory anyway.<br /> <br /> Part of his skill as a choreographer was in his ability to make that look plausible; to make the frantic, flailing goof with the constant look of trepidation genuinely look like he was winning out over superior fighters through supplementing skill with sheer, unrelenting determination.<br /> <br /> (Another part of that choreography skill is in making people who might often be technically inferior martial artists look better)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">when they die to Dawns it's probably because they got their cushioned behinds handed to them in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly.<br /> <br /> That probably generally goes a <b><i>bit</i></b> differently than &quot;I use my archery to instantly kill about three of them before any can get within attack range&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your Dawn is going to have to fuggin' <i>earn</i> those victories, I think.<br /> <br /> I mean Jesus Christ, did we all forget the playtester reports about people with characters who were able to get in one hit kills <i>once</i>, at great expense on the occasion when it worked, and inviting disaster every time it didn't?<br /> <br /> &quot;Aha, you foolish lesser Exalted, watch as I pour Essence into my mighty shaft that I might loose it upon one of you with such force as to reduce you to a greasy smear!&quot;<br /> &quot;Shit, he killed Larry before he could do anything! We may give our lives here, but it is our sacred duty to continue regardless.&quot;<br /> &quot;Actually... I'm kind of spent, and even a bit sleepy. I was sort of hoping that opening barrage would be enough to satisfy you, and then you would just go home&quot;.<br /> &quot;.....&quot;<br /> &quot;.....&quot;<br /> &quot;We're going to break all of your hands and feet, put a sack soaked in pitch over your head, and light it on fire.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T02:55:10-07:00","id":685386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685360#post685360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think Raziere is probably right about it being more of a story difference (ie who is and isn't an extra) rather than a metaphysical one, but sometimes writers forgot that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a middle stripe between heroic and extra! Some of the writers forgot, ignored, or fought against it, but it was <i>there</i>! &quot;Heroic&quot; <i>was</i> a quality that extended beyond the nature of the story, straight into the mechanics - which is why I'm fighting against it! It was something that could be granted or taken away by Charms; it changed the way your dice rolls worked, even!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T04:39:26-07:00","id":685471,"title":"","content":"The only constant thing your number of dots means is how many dice you add to relevant rolls and what Charms you can learn (if you have access to Charms at all). What it translates to on character level should be the business of the player and the Storyteller. Trying to nail it down in terms of &quot;X dots means this, Y dots means that, and only one in Z people will have this many dots&quot; is more trouble than it's worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T04:48:17-07:00","id":685483,"title":"","content":"very angry right now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T05:18:10-07:00","id":685534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685483#post685483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">very angry right now</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it something I said?<br /> <br /> EDIT: No but seriously if I said something dumb I blame having had three hours of sleep since Wednesday morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-02-2015, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T05:32:35-07:00","id":685567,"title":"","content":"Darn it, I shouldn't have brought up the thing with the pitch sack... it's going to be very difficult to resist the impulse to turn this thread into a list of all the things vengeful Wyld Hunts have inflicted upon Solars* who they managed to subdue short of immediate death, but not before the Anathema had the gall to fight back so well that it killed several hunters and bloodied the rest.<br /> <br /> Note to self: have scenes revolving around some kind of Dynastic party include one of the elders bringing out the pride of his collection; the mummified nose he got to take off of some Solar because he cast the best lots for divvying up trophies.<br /> <br /> * And probably Lunars as well, but I think the slow death and mutilation of a Solar would be more stark in how so many people tend to be so up on their supposed inherent dignity. I don't think many things say &quot;dying like a chump&quot; to people who would use that phrase than being tied down like Gulliver until you simply dehydrate to death while the hunters just sit to the side watching you (and occasionally smashing at you with hammers to keep you too weak and broken to move), and then having your killers roll dice to see who gets your ears and nose and hands as a souvenir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T23:41:29-07:00","id":686610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685380#post685380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jackie Chan characters are the protagonists of his films.<br /> <br /> (Another part of that choreography skill is in making people who might often be technically inferior martial artists look better)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that je ne sais quoi might be a Solar exaltation in the context of exalted<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=685380#post685380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly.<br /> <br /> That probably generally goes a <b><i>bit</i></b> differently than &quot;I use my archery to instantly kill about three of them before any can get within attack range&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your Dawn is going to have to fuggin' <i>earn</i> those victories, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I said kill three before they close to range, if they do at all, I didn't mean it like the Solar is standing on a hill and fires off three shots, killing three DBs in the time it takes them to run into close range. I was thinking more like a Solar fighting smart and using things like Forceful Arrow to send her opponents pinwheeling backwards into terrain features while pulling back or clipping their ankles to render them hobbled and vulnerable. That's not even counting what happens if they've got Solar style athletics or dodge or stealth or awareness or ride anything like that.<br /> <br /> Also I know there isn't anything in the current Solar charmset that allows them to do things like shoot enemy's arrows out of the air with their own arrows, but there <i>really </i>should be. It's almost a staple of fictional archers, from Robin Hood to Tauriel.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The Solar absolutely has to fuggin' earn those victories, but that doesn't mean bending over backwards and trying to manipulate everything to their favor to do it, it just means they can't coast there way through 5 Shikari the way they could with 5 random mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T01:09:37-07:00","id":686668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that je ne sais quoi might be a Solar exaltation in the context of exalted</div> </div> </div> </div> That is my point. That is part of why Dawns can be something other than the best fighters ever. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I said kill three before they close to range, if they do at all, I didn't mean it like the Solar is standing on a hill and fires off three shots, killing three DBs in the time it takes them to run into close range. I was thinking more like a Solar fighting smart and using things like Forceful Arrow to send her opponents pinwheeling backwards into terrain features while pulling back or clipping their ankles to render them hobbled and vulnerable. That's not even counting what happens if they've got Solar style athletics or dodge or stealth or awareness or ride anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, that sounds more like what writers and playtesters have been talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T12:46:11-07:00","id":687407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded?p=686668#post686668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That is my point. That is part of why Dawns can be something other than the best fighters ever. Yes, that sounds more like what writers and playtesters have been talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay cool, I think we are in agreement then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T20:23:55-07:00","id":693398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/682380-man-i-love-dragon-blooded#post682380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am specifically talking about Dragon-Blooded of the Blessed Realm who are part of a House. Outcastes are okay, but not half as interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just MO, but I disagree. One of the things I like most about outcaste Dragon-Blooded is that they can allow you to play with one of the Solars' greatest strengths, their &quot;Vanilla&quot;-quality, AND allow you to be as openly Heroic as you like with complete legitimacy! In short, you can be as over-the-top badass as you can manage, and no one's gonna call the Wyld Hunt on your show-off ass for doing so! <br /> <br /> I also like the notion of outcaste DBs naturally finding one another, and discovering for themselves through trial and error how their powers interact, rather than being raised and trained to do so. And I think the scene of outcastes, either singly or as a group, running into a Dynastic/Lookshyan Brotherhood, with all the advantages that gives them, can be played out in multiple ways.<br /> <br /> Not saying that I dislike Realm DBs, just that outcastes are a different flavor of Terrestrial, and not necessarily an inferior one!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T00:37:22-07:00","id":693528,"title":"","content":"Outcastes do have to grapple with the politics of the Realm, and how it sees them and would draw them in, or sideline them, and Celestials who would do the same, but... it's very different to being Anathema.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they can be preferable heroes if people are interested in the idea of heroes who could come from anywhere, and be anyone, and yet are not keen on the Prophesied One / Biblical Heroes on a mission from God vibes that the Solars throw off, preferring The One Who Chooses to The Chosen One.<br /> <br /> They do *sort* of discard a lot of the interesting dualities between Solars and Dragonblooded that hippokrene touches on though, so I can see why they might seem a bit &quot;cake and eat it&quot; to some though, and so less interesting (plus the lower power they have).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}